  "$comment": "Distribution ids used in shield.toml (affected.fixes[].distro, versions[].lines[].distros). tracker is the vendor source the fixes rows are read from; {cve} is replaced by the CVE id. os_release, uname_regex, uname_not_regex, compare, line_guard and packages say how a host matches the distro and how its running kernel is compared with fixed (tools/export-registry copies them into each package's distro_fixes): os_release.id lists /etc/os-release IDs (the RHEL rows' data is Red Hat's errata, so RHEL and Rocky match them too), version_id matches VERSION_ID exactly or as its major (\"9\" matches 9.4), variant_id VARIANT_ID; uname_regex/uname_not_regex (POSIX ERE) pick the kernel flavour from uname -r; compare is dpkg (dpkg --compare-versions on the running kernel package's version), rpm (rpmvercmp on its version-release), pacman (vercmp on the Arch package's version, e.g. 7.3.5.arch1-1; Arch's linux package follows upstream stable, its tracker lists only some CVEs, so the first fixed package is the first one built from the upstream release with the fix, per the package's git tags) or os-version (VERSION from os-release, dotted numeric); line_guard true: a first fixed version counts only for a running kernel of the same major.minor line (an HWE or backports kernel is another package); packages are the kernel packages whose version is compared.",
